===Etymology 2===
Either from {{inh|en|enm|been|pos=infinitive||to be}} (from {{inh|en|ang|bēon}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|be|en<id:infinitive><pos:infinitive ending>}}), or from a dialectal use of the preceding past tense form as an infinitive form (compare dialectal use of {{m|en|I's|(I)'s}}, {{m|en|is|(I) is}} in the first person, {{m|en|am|(he) am}} in the third person, etc).

